.TH JELLYFIN-WAKE-HDD 8 "September 2026" "jellyfin-wake-hdd" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
jellyfin-wake-hdd \- keep NAS drives spinning while Jellyfin clients are connected
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jellyfin-wake-hdd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jellyfin-wake-hdd
queries the Jellyfin API for currently connected client sessions
(including clients that are connected but idle, not only ones actively
playing). If at least
.I MIN_SESSIONS
sessions are present, it runs
.BR stat (1)
on each path listed in
.I WAKE_PATHS
to force the underlying drives or enclosure to spin up, preventing them
from hitting their own idle spin-down timeout while someone may start
playback at any moment.
.PP
It takes no arguments and is intended to be run periodically by
jellyfin-wake-hdd.timer,
not invoked directly, though running it by hand is useful for testing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/jellyfin-wake-hdd.conf
Configuration file; see
.BR jellyfin-wake-hdd.conf (5).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits non\-zero if the config file is missing or incomplete, or if the
Jellyfin API cannot be reached or returns something unparseable. Each
run's outcome is written to standard output/error, which
.B systemd
captures in the journal
(\fBjournalctl -u jellyfin-wake-hdd.service\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jellyfin-wake-hdd.conf (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
